*.pyc
.venv/
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
*.egg-info/
# Agent workspaces (docs/framework/dispatch.md §1.2) and the scratch an agent
# leaves beside them. `jj` skips other workspaces' roots but snapshots
# everything else on every command, so unignored scratch here is committed
# rather than merely untracked; `git` skips nothing and sees the workspaces too.
# Two paths under it are the repository's own and tracked: the role
# definitions and the project settings Claude Code reads from a clone
# (AGENTS.md). The pattern names the directory's children rather than the
# directory, because a directory that is ignored is never entered, and a `!`
# inside it could not bring anything back.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/agents/
!/.claude/settings.json
# Every workstation slot: the seed kit, the cached Pulumi passphrase, the
# account roots' token files, the state backend's client bundle
# (docs/credentials.md §1 rule 6). One directory, one line, one thing on this
# machine that is secret.
.credentials/
# Names workstation secrets had before `.credentials/`. Nothing reads them;
# they stay ignored so that a copy left at the root is never snapshotted into
# a change -- `jj` tracks every file it is not told to ignore.
.pulumi.secret
.github.token
# Dumps of the Pulumi state. `state-backend dump` writes one into the working
# directory by default, and a converge that replaces the box writes one before
# it terminates anything -- both are usually run from the repository root, and
# both hold every stack's state under `age`. This repository is public.
*.dump.age
# What a `file://` backend writes beside a committed checkpoint and keeps on
# the machine that ran it (framework/pulumi.md §3.3): the copy of the previous
# checkpoint every save leaves, the update history, the backup copies, and the
# lock a run holds. Only `meta.yaml` and each stack's `<stack>.json` travel.
# The `operator-stack` driver's record of a check that failed or never
# finished is the workstation's too: it names what a run found, for that run's
# operator to act on.
/checkpoints/.pulumi/stacks/**/*.bak
/checkpoints/.pulumi/history/
/checkpoints/.pulumi/backups/
/checkpoints/.pulumi/locks/
/checkpoints/*.failed-check
